  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-blockquote-element\r\n\r\nThis element's content model specifies flow content, which includes h1-h6. But it's unclear to me how and if I should use them.\r\n\r\nFor example, if I'm quoting a part of a document that has headers, how do I mark up those headers? Should I start back at h1, or use the next level down? Should I use headers at all, as they add to the document outline despite the quoted document not actually being part of the document?\r\n\r\nIn the context I've encountered this, it needs to be a (block)quote, as it was part of fan fiction. I can't opt to include it as part of the content.\r\n\r\nI hope I'm making sense here. :)",
